# web/dist holds the real frontend build, embedded via go:embed only in
# builds tagged -tags embed (see web/embed_real.go / web/embed_stub.go and
# design doc §7). 100% ignored, no exceptions — a plain (untagged) build
# never requires this directory to contain anything, so a local frontend
# build here never touches any git-tracked file. The user-facing
# placeholder page lives at web/placeholder.html instead, tracked normally
# since it's outside this directory entirely.
web/dist/

# wrangler local cache for the Cloudflare Worker under deploy/
.wrangler/
.superpowers/

gui-test-screenshots/
# Article drafts and their assets stay local. Scoped to this one subdirectory
# on purpose: a bare "docs/" also swallows docs/screenshots/, which README.md
# and README_zh.md embed, so every future screenshot would go missing from the
# project page with no local signal that it was never committed.
/docs/articles/
.zcode/

# docker-compose's default bind-mount target (all container state: generated
# config + SQLite database) when compose is run from a repo checkout.
/yolorouter/
